  "summary": "Lead Software Engineer with over 17 years of experience in software engineering, enterprise systems, and information technology supporting government and mission-critical environments.\n\nMy background spans full stack software development, application modernization, database design, cloud-ready architectures, DevOps workflows, and technical leadership. I specialize in building and modernizing enterprise applications using ASP.NET Core, .NET, C#, Web APIs, Entity Framework Core, SQL Server, Docker, SignalR, Azure, and GitLab CI/CD pipelines.\n\nI currently lead and mentor software engineers within fully remote Agile development environments, where I conduct code reviews, lead technical discussions, support modernization initiatives, and help train development teams on AI-assisted software engineering workflows using tools such as Claude, GPT-5, and local LLM technologies.\n\nEarlier in my career, I supported aviation and database administration environments where precision, reliability, and attention to detail were critical. That experience helped shape my approach to developing secure, scalable, and dependable enterprise software solutions.\n\nIn addition to engineering leadership, I have extensive experience creating technical documentation, onboarding materials, software tutorials, and end-user training resources. I enjoy helping others understand complex technical concepts and bridging the gap between theory and practical real-world implementation.\n\nAreas of interest include:\n• Full Stack Development\n• Enterprise Software Engineering\n• ASP.NET Core & .NET\n• AI-Assisted Development\n• Software Architecture & Modernization\n• Cloud & DevOps Technologies\n• Database Design & Development\n• Software Testing & Quality Assurance\n• Technical Mentorship & Training\n• Online Learning & Adult Education\n\nM.S. in Information Technology, Southern New Hampshire University\nActive Secret Security Clearance",
